{#
    The footer of a player's Results list (docs/features/navigation README §4.7, PROF-05b): "Showing N of M", Show more
    and Show all. Every control is a real link - `?page=N` renders rows 1…50·N, so they work without JavaScript, a
    reload keeps the rows and Back finds them again; the page's script (player_results_controller.js) appends the next
    rows instead of loading the page (Show more: the `fragment=more` stream) or reloads only the list (Show all).

    Show all (`?page=` the last page) only while the tab has at most PlayerResultsPage::SHOW_ALL_MAX rows. Above that the
    player gets "Export your results" on their own Results, every other viewer nothing more (Show more stays).

    Show more's stream replaces this element, so it is rendered (empty) once every row is shown.

    Input: results (PlayerResultsPage)
#}
<div id="player-results-more" data-nosnippet>
    {% if results.hasMore %}
        {% set list = results.listCriteria %}
        {% set route_params = {playerId: results.playerId} %}
        <div class="d-flex flex-column align-items-center gap-2 mt-3 mb-4">
            <p class="text-body-secondary fs-sm mb-0" data-testid="results-shown">
                {{ 'profile.results_shown'|trans({'%shown%': results.shownRowsCount|plain_number, '%total%': results.rowsCount|plain_number}) }}
            </p>
            <div class="d-flex flex-wrap justify-content-center gap-2">
                <a class="btn btn-outline-primary btn-sm" href="{{ path('player_results', route_params|merge(list.withPage(results.page + 1).toQuery)) }}" data-results-more data-action="player-results#more">
                    {{ 'puzzle_times.leaderboard.show_more'|trans({'%count%': results.moreCount}) }}
                </a>
                {% if results.canShowAll %}
                    <a class="btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm" href="{{ path('player_results', route_params|merge(list.withPage(results.lastPage).toQuery)) }}" data-results-all data-action="player-results#all">
                        {{ 'puzzle_times.leaderboard.show_all'|trans({'%count%': results.rowsCount|plain_number}) }}
                    </a>
                {% elseif logged_user.profile is not null and logged_user.profile.playerId is same as results.playerId %}
                    {# Too many rows for one page: the whole history is one download away (docs/features/data-export.md) #}
                    <a class="btn btn-link btn-sm" href="{{ path('export_puzzler_data', {playerId: results.playerId}) }}" data-results-export>
                        <i class="bi bi-download me-1" aria-hidden="true"></i>{{ 'player_results.export_results'|trans }}
                    </a>
                {% endif %}
            </div>
        </div>
    {% endif %}
</div>
